== a disabled builtin yields to PATH:
program echo hi
file
-c:2:9: error: Builtin `builtin`: 'echo' is not a shell builtin.
builtin status=1
enable -n echo
echo
file
builtin
file
back
builtin
== each builtin word is a separate entry:
[ stays
-c:2:1: error: The command 'test' was not found.
test status=127
test
test
== -s lists only special builtins:
export listed
trap listed
source listed
echo omitted
cd omitted
== listings are sorted and -a marks disabled entries:
enable .|enable :|enable [
enable -n test
cd
test
enable .
== loadable builtins are not supported:
-c:1:11: error: Builtin `enable`: 'echo' is not dynamically loaded.
-c:1:16: error: Builtin `enable`: 'nosuch' is not a shell builtin.
delete status=1
-c:2:11: error: Builtin `enable`: Loadable builtins are not supported.
load status=1
== a disabled builtin expands redirections as a program:
builtin a=/dev/null
program b=
command c=
== a disabled special builtin is an ordinary command:
-c:1:19: error: The command 'export' was not found.
the shell continues
== a bundled utility is enabled and disabled by name:
-c:1:1: error: The command 'basename' was not found.
status=127
b
builtin
basename
-c:3:21: error: The command 'basename' was not found.
enable -n basename
b
== the kosh mood disables a reachable utility:
b
status=1
== an unknown name fails:
-c:1:8: error: Builtin `enable`: 'nosuchbuiltin' is not a shell builtin.
status=1
